<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Sequani</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.) · capital Vesontio</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of Franche-Comté whose rivalry with the Aedui led them to invite the German Ariovistus into Gaul.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Sequani lived between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saone">Saône</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jura-mountains">Jura</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, around their great oppidum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besancon">Vesontio</a> (<a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/imperial-city-of-besancon">Besançon</a>) in a loop of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/doubs">Doubs</a>. Their land was famous for salted pork exported to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>They contested with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aedui">Aedui</a> for control of tolls on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saone">Saône</a> and for leadership of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. Caesar names Catamantaloedes as a former king who held the title of friend of the Roman people, and his son Casticus as a would-be king.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>To defeat the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aedui">Aedui</a> they hired the German leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariovistus">Ariovistus</a>, who then seized a third of their land, until Caesar drove him out in 58 BCE. The Sequani joined the revolt of 52 BCE. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besancon">Vesontio</a> became an important town, and their land later formed the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maxima-sequanorum">Maxima Sequanorum</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sequani.jpg" alt="Sequani" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sequani_hemi_stater_Gallica_celtiques_1505_avers.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 51 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vesontio</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Catamantaloedes, Casticus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>France</dd></dl></aside></div>

